XQUERY OPERATIONS
-----------------

1. Display all books

for $book in /library/books/book
return $book


2. Display all students

for $student in /library/students/student
return $student


3. Display only book titles

for $book in /library/books/book
return $book/title


4. Display names of students from IT department

for $student in /library/students/student
where $student/department = "IT"
return $student/name


5. LET operation

let $students := /library/students/student
return $students/name


6. WHERE operation

for $student in /library/students/student
where $student/department = "IT"
return $student/name


7. ORDER BY operation

for $book in /library/books/book
order by xs:integer($book/publish)
return $book/title


8. RETURN operation

for $book in /library/books/book
return $book/title


9. Combined FLWOR query

for $student in /library/students/student
let $dept := $student/department
where $dept = "IT"
order by $student/name
return $student/name


10. Join operation

NOTE:
The original Assignment 5 XML does not contain an issuedBook element.
Therefore, a student-book join cannot be performed using the original XML.

If issuedBook is added inside student, for example:

<issuedBook>101</issuedBook>

then the following join query can be used:

for $student in /library/students/student
for $book in /library/books/book
where $student/issuedBook = $book/@id
return
    <issue>
        <student>{data($student/name)}</student>
        <book>{data($book/title)}</book>
    </issue>
